# pkg/

Install-time artifacts intended for packaging on modern systemd-based distros (Debian 13+, Ubuntu 24.04+, RHEL 10+, CentOS Stream 10+, etc.).

## What’s included (common)

### Provisioning script

- `/usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-provision-user`
  - Creates, for an end user `<u>`:
    - system user: `@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>`
    - private group: `@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>`
    - shared group: `@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>-shared`
    - `/home/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>/shared` (2770, setgid) workspace root
    - `/home/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>/tmp` (0700)
    - sudoers drop-in allowing members of `@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>-shared` to run
      `/usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/run-as-@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-<u>`

Example:

```bash
sudo /usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-provision-user <username>
# log out/in for group membership to take effect
```

## Notes

- `/usr/lib/...` is used for vendor-supplied sysusers/tmpfiles/systemd units. `/etc/...` is reserved for admin overrides.
- Packaging should ensure `/etc/sudoers.d/*` drop-ins are `root:root` and `0440`.
- Wrapper scripts under `/usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/` should be `root:root` and executable.
